# Template for .env — the gitignored, per-host local environment file.
#
#   cp .env.template .env
#
# Two readers, and nothing else:
#
#   - the VS Code debug adapter, via "envFile" in .vscode/launch.json. A missing
#     file is silently ignored there, so this is optional.
#   - a plain shell:  set -a; . ./.env; set +a
#
# The systemd unit does NOT read it — that reads
# /etc/booking-buddy/credentials.env, see bot/systemd/credentials.env.example.
#
# ---- THE ONE RULE ------------------------------------------------------------
# Comment a variable out; do not set it to an empty value. Most of these are
# read with `??` or `Number()`, and "" is not nullish, so a blank line is not the
# same as absent:
#
#   LOG_PATH=             -> logs land in the repo root, not log/
#   NAV_TIMEOUT_MS=       -> Number("") is 0, so every navigation times out
#   COURTRESERVE_ORG_ID=  -> broken CourtReserve URLs
#   AUTH_PATH=            -> setStorageState("") throws
#
# Only COURTRESERVE_* (trimmed) and PLAYWRIGHT_DEBUG_PORT (truthiness) treat a
# blank value as "not set".
#
# ---- Credentials -------------------------------------------------------------
# Unattended re-login. Both are needed together; a blank one counts as absent and
# the client falls back to the interactive manual-login prompt. Mainly for the
# Pi, where nothing can answer that prompt. Never log the password.
# COURTRESERVE_USERNAME=you@example.com
# COURTRESERVE_PASSWORD=
#
# ---- Watching a run on a headless host ----------------------------------------
# To see the browser on a Pi (no display), start these in their own terminals
# first — .env cannot start them, it can only point at the result:
#
#   Xvfb :99 -screen 0 1280x900x24 -ac &
#   x11vnc -display :99 -forever -shared -nopw -rfbport 5900 &
#
# Then a VNC client on your laptop connects to <pi-ip>:5900. In this file:
#
# DISPLAY=:99
# PLAYWRIGHT_DEBUG_PORT=9222
#
# Chromium binds 9222 to loopback, so it is not reachable over the LAN. Tunnel
# it from the laptop — this command then sits there doing nothing:
#
#   ssh -L 9222:localhost:9222 <user>@<pi>
#
# and open http://localhost:9222 in the laptop's browser. Leave DISPLAY unset on
# a desktop that already has a screen.
#
# Stop the Pi's timer before a debug run, or they contend for my-profile/:
#   sudo systemctl stop booking-buddy.timer
#
# ---- Headless ----------------------------------------------------------------
# The library defaults to headless; the examples/ force a visible window
# regardless. Only set this to run the library headful on a host with a display.
# HEADLESS=false
#
# ---- Paths -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Where the saved session and the persistent profile live. Relative to the
# directory you launch from (the repo root, both for js-debug and the unit).
# AUTH_PATH=./auth.json
# PROFILE_DIR=./my-profile
#
# ---- Bot logging -------------------------------------------------------------
# Directory for bot-<date>.log and booking-buddy-<date>.log. Relative names land
# under the cwd; an absolute path wins over --log-path. Set false on the library
# side (ClientOptions.logPath) to disable the library's own file entirely.
# LOG_PATH=./log
# LOG_LEVEL=debug
#
# ---- Tuning (defaults shown) -------------------------------------------------
# MIN_ACTION_DELAY_MS=1000
# MAX_ACTION_DELAY_MS=3000
# NAV_TIMEOUT_MS=60000
# NAV_RETRIES=1
#
# ---- CourtReserve ------------------------------------------------------------
# Organization id; the default matches Bellevue Badminton Club.
# COURTRESERVE_ORG_ID=7031
# PORT=3000